{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4c7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07a40-291a-7b50-9359-ce2838523baf"},"sequence":190,"recorded_at":1780531400000375,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5c56535d-a447-4a6e-a8da-9b382d4b9205","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5c56535d-a447-4a6e-a8da-9b382d4b9205","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5c56535d-a447-4a6e-a8da-9b382d4b9205"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"ca959f11-c31d-4313-8bda-b8a7f280375f"},"task_id":"ca959f11-c31d-4313-8bda-b8a7f280375f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"ca959f11-c31d-4313-8bda-b8a7f280375f","chunk":"Read text file `internal/provhost/profile_agreement_test.go`.\n1|package provhost\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"reflect\"\n5|\t\"testing\"\n6|\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/provider\"\n8|)\n9|\n10|// TestBuiltinsEqualProfileProviders pins the cross-package agreement\n11|// between the two hand-written six-provider literals directly: the\n12|// Section 7.1 built-in registry behind provider.Builtins and the\n13|// Section 7.7 provider registry behind profileProviders. It reads no\n14|// SPEC.md line, so the agreement no longer runs only transitively\n15|// through the two derivations' different line windows (provider's\n16|// TestSection71BuiltinRegistryIsDocumentOrder against Section 7.1,\n17|// this package's TestProfileYOLOMappingIsDerivedFromSpec against the\n18|// Section 7.7 table).\n19|//\n20|// Set agreement already has a direct pin:\n21|// TestSixProviderSetMatchesDiscoveryRegistry balances the two sets.\n22|// That pin is order-insensitive, so a reorder on exactly one side\n23|// leaves the whole suite green — the remaining structural hole. This\n24|// test closes it with an order-sensitive comparison: both orders are\n25|// independently spec-pinned (Section 7.1 listed order is the discovery\n26|// enumeration order, Section 7.7 table order is the profile registry\n27|// order), so ordered equality holds today, and a seventh member, a\n28|// rename, a removal, or a reorder on either side alone reddens here.\n29|// A future spec bump that legitimately reorders one table must\n30|// consciously revisit this agreement rather than drift through a\n31|// set-only check.\n32|func TestBuiltinsEqualProfileProviders(t *testing.T) {\n33|\tt.Parallel()\n34|\n35|\tgot := provider.Builtins()\n36|\tif !reflect.DeepEqual(got, profileProviders) {\n37|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"provider.Builtins() = %v, want provhost profileProviders %v: the two six-provider literals disagree without a spec change\", got, profileProviders)\n38|\t}\n39|}"}}}
