g at all three arms (BackendID echo + Error() render). Red-before: new test 6/6 FAIL; post-fix 7/7 PASS (exit 0).\n+- FINDING (census): all 31 BackendID-carrying refusal sites now validated — 27 in terminalbackend.go + 4 in manifest.go (probe arms via ParseProbe admission, manifest arms via ParseManifest admission + Resolve re-validation). Sibling packages measured, NOT changed (sibling suites pin their refusal text: secprim env_test asserts the echo verbatim): environ unknown-member echoes the full wire key (269B refusal, Error()-rendered, LIVE); secprim BuildEnv env-name echoes the full refused name (259B, LIVE); secprim paths truncate to 64 chars via memberErrorTarget (bounded, deliberate); secprim argv echoes positions only (clean); provhost Error() never echoes (static messages; identifiers travel in Details, inert + 16KiB ValidateDetails cap). The two LIVE sites are stated bounds with entry points, escaping content, and owner (sibling-suite pins) — follow-up leaves, not this diff.\n+- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-2okwyf_outcome-r2.md` + `battery_2okwyf_r2.json` (5 applied/5 killed/0 survived: narrowing 2 incl. length-gated + reorder, arm-deletion 1, census-only 1, audit-only 1 naming terminalbackend.go:651; NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct rows; masks 15/243/665 all non-empty; mutant bodies in JSON). Round-1 battery anchors all still present (grep-verified); round-1 outcome/battery resources stand for unchanged code. Candidate tree OID in the outcome doc, detached-index write-tree AFTER the LOGBOOK append.\n+- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (all ok), `-race` terminalbackend exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (tb 95.1%, ph 86.0%, pv 97.8%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, `go build` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean.\n+- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\n+\n+### 0839 — 2okwyf: A5/A7/A8/A9/F-B1 closed (cross-package agreement, trust asymmetry, three nits, digit-guard sentence)\n"}}}
